# Force LF line endings on shell scripts that are exec'd inside Linux containers.
# Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) corrupts the shebang and
# every subsequent line — `env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` on boot.
# Bit us once on 2026-05-01 (image f54a1081f432, entrypoint.sh + healthcheck.sh).
docker/live/*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Crucible CRU-1 moat: `crucible.version.gates_hash()` is a SHA-256 over the RAW BYTES of a
# gates YAML (deliberately — so any edit, even a comment, is visible in a run's provenance). That
# makes the hash line-ending-sensitive, so a stock Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) silently
# moves EVERY frozen hash: signal_eval 519158fa1450 -> d04d7e747b48, and likewise for the Taiwan and
# small-cap probe seals. Two consequences, both bad: the three CRU-1 tripwires in
# tests/crucible/test_version.py go red for a reason that has nothing to do with the gates (inviting
# someone to "fix" them by re-pinning the constants, which would destroy the anti-goal-post-move
# seal outright), and the gates_hash stamped into a run_manifest/DiscoveryCard differs by platform,
# so `crucible reproduce` cannot verify a run across OSes. Pin these to LF so the seal is a property
# of the gate content, not of the checkout host. Same failure mode as the shell scripts above.
configs/*.gates.yaml text eol=lf

# Files copied verbatim into Linux containers (Dockerfile COPY, busybox crond)
# must stay LF — busybox crond chokes on CRLF in /etc/crontabs/root and
# `docker build` will silently bake CRLF shebangs into intermediate images.
docker/live/**/Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker/live/**/Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
docker/live/**/crontab text eol=lf
docker/live/**/*_crontab text eol=lf
